  {
    "platform": "tiktok",
    "account": "pierluigibarcaa",
    "url": "https://www.tiktok.com/@pierluigibarcaa/video/7676424163959082272",
    "thumbnail": "https://p19-common-sign.tiktokcdn-us.com/tos-useast2a-p-0037-euttp/o831RABIEBBiAC9ifCAoI2AioBIOrIRGx23ITI~tplv-tiktokx-origin.image?dr=9636&x-expires=1788364800&x-signature=ZgcHTiP0fPJCRbVpQqQbuDizJGg%3D&t=4d5b0474&ps=13740610&shp=81f88b70&shcp=43f4a2f9&idc=useast5",
    "video": "",
    "carousel_urls": [],
    "format": "TikTok",
    "caption": "Drone movements to make your shots feel more cinematic. \ud83d\ude81\ud83c\udfac It\u2019s not just about flying the drone \u2014 the movement you choose can completely change the way you tell a story. Parallax Move sideways while keeping your subject in frame. It creates depth and separation between the foreground and background. Expanding Orbit Orbit around your subject while gradually moving away. Perfect for revealing the environment and creating a sense of scale. Reveal Push Push forward while passing behind or beyond a foreground element. A great way to build anticipation and reveal the scene. Tilt Reveal Combine vertical movement with a camera tilt to gradually reveal what\u2019s beyond the frame. Top Down Spiral Combine a top-down perspective with a spiral movement. Perfect for creating a dynamic and hypnotic shot. Save this for your next flight. \ud83d\ude81 Which one would you try first? #portugal #dronemovements #dji #djimavic4pro  @DJI Official",
